  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "During Apollo 11, the first Moon landing in 1969, the astronaut Buzz Aldrin was told that if anything happened to Neil Armstrong when Armstrong stepped outside, Aldrin was not to play the hero and try to save him. The documentary filmmaker James Fox tells this as something a woman named Fay Ann Potter told him. It is told as a sign of how much was quietly planned and kept from the public around the landing."
